From e074291c45ac71a08b812395ceec40692d8a59cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:01:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: Reference (BT.2390) as the default tone mapping of
 every profile

The tone mapping method of a reference display (BT.2390) has been the
documented default since it was added, but a new profile got Off.
CVideoSettings starts with Off; CSettings::Load() of a profile without a
settings file of its own calls Reset(), which saves the defaults before
they are read, and that file said hadestonemap 1, so the Off stayed.
LibreELEC and Kodi profiles had Off as well (Kodi's own new profiles get it
the same way), and the earlier migration only turned Hable into BT.2390. On
a display or projector without HDR, Off leaves HDR10, HDR10+, HLG and Dolby
Vision profiles 7 and 8.1 unmapped (washed out), and "Play HDR videos as
SDR" sends HDR unmapped on one with HDR. A display that is sent HDR is not
concerned: the method maps only what goes out as SDR. YBLOD described the
fault (its kodi-9909 and kodi-9960); seen in QEMU with the image of
00f60f1: a new profile is written with tonemapmethod 0 and hadestonemap 1.

- CMediaSettings starts its defaults with BT.2390 (CVideoSettings itself,
  which Kodi makes for other purposes too, keeps Off), so the file of a new
  profile is written with it.
- An Off saved with hadestonemap below 2 becomes BT.2390, once, with a line
  in kodi.log; the file is written with hadestonemap 2 from then on, and an
  Off chosen after that stays. (An Off that a user chose under 1.0 is lost
  once; the log says so.)
- The video settings that Kodi keeps for a file (the settings table of the
  video database, written whenever a video stops with any of them other
  than the defaults, another audio or subtitle stream being enough) took
  the Off along. They are looked at once per profile, before the settings
  of the first video are read: Off becomes BT.2390, with the count in
  kodi.log; a method chosen for a file (Hable, say) stays. guisettings.xml
  says it is done (hadestonemapfiles 1); a failed update is tried again
  with the next video. Not for settings without the defaults at all: what
  Kodi reads before it makes the file of a new profile (seen in QEMU: "unable
  to load settings ... creating new default settings" follows it).
- A tone mapping method out of range is no longer clamped to
  VS_TONEMAPMETHOD_MAX, which names no method (the formatter of the log
  throws for it): the default is taken instead.

The decisions are in ToneMapDefault.h, tested on the host through a
sequence of files saved and read (a new profile, one of 1.0, one of
LibreELEC, Off chosen afterwards, values out of range, a file without the
defaults), with nine mutants, each caught. In QEMU (00f60f1 with this
kodi.bin bound over its own): a profile and kept settings written by the
image's Kodi become BT.2390 with their two lines in kodi.log, a Hable kept
for a file stays, an Off chosen afterwards stays (for the profile and for
a file), and a new profile is written with BT.2390, 2 and 1 and says
nothing.
